<h1>About Agent Built</h1>

<p>Agent Built is a working notebook from someone shipping software with AI agents in 2026. Not a course. Not a newsletter that sells you the course. A place where the things that work get written down so other people building can use them.</p>

<h2>What we cover</h2>

<ul>
  <li>How to integrate Claude, ChatGPT, and other agents with the rest of your stack — n8n, Make, Zapier, custom code.</li>
  <li>What we tried, what worked, what didn't, with the receipts.</li>
  <li>Specific pricing, scaling, and tooling tradeoffs (because nobody is publishing the actual numbers).</li>
  <li>Tools we've built ourselves — when relevant, when honest.</li>
</ul>

<h2>How posts get written</h2>

<p>Some posts on Agent Built are co-written with AI agents. We think it would be weird to run an "Agent Built" blog and pretend otherwise. The pipeline: we pick a topic, the agent does the research (real sources, real benchmarks), drafts a post, and a human reads every word before it goes live. Nothing here is unreviewed. We tell you this because the alternative is dishonest.</p>

<h2>Who's behind it</h2>

<p>Operated by a software engineer / operator running multiple AI-product experiments in public. We're not selling a $1,997 course. If a post is paid placement we'll say so inline.</p>

<h2>Contact</h2>
<p>For corrections, tips, or work: hello@agent-built.com</p>

